Title: F1-M08 — The Long Night (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. PLATEAU DUGOUT - NIGHT

[[AMBIENCE: wind over the rim, a lantern guttering, distant artillery]]
[[MUSIC: sparse, held tension]]

A map of the plateau is pinned to a plank wall with bayonets. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(serious)
Hold the plateau until dawn. The relief column says it will approach from the east.

MIRA
(measured)
That signal matches the enemy's old cipher. We cannot assume it is genuine.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: plateau base with ore field inside the wire, richer hollow below the north rim, approach lanes north, east and south, western pass and gorge, enemy camp in the valley]]

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(firm)
Defend the plateau, verify the relief signal, and keep the western pass open. If the eastern column is hostile, do not chase it into the valley.

MIRA
(dry)
Twenty-two minutes to dawn. Their factories run all night. Each wave will be heavier than the last, and the ore inside the wire will not pay for it.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(pointing at map)
The hollow below the north rim has the ore. It is also on the north lane. Work it if you can hold it.

MIRA
(analytical)
Any column that reaches the ramp gets the challenge. A correct response is proof. Our colours on a truck are paint.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(short)
Three lanes, towers on two. Keep a reserve for the third. Nothing goes down the east road.

MIRA
(concerned)
One signal from the east, nothing from the west. If relief is coming at all, I would like to know why it has only one voice.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
